From a8e49931cc41388bbd7bb20ce4a82ac5b7808210 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: professorpalmer <professorpalmer@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 12:27:44 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 77/79] cuda: bound the one-column mat-vec rows by the row
 count, not by stride_col_dst

With ids at one column (decode MUL_MAT_ID) the expert slots are channels and stride_col_dst is nrows * n_used.
With the small-K geometry (rows per block = nwarps) the last row block of a slot passed the bound and stored
rows past nrows into the first rows of the next slot, which that slot's first block also writes: a race, a
different error each run (test-backend-ops MUL_MAT_ID PTQ1_0 / PQ2_0, m=70, n=1, k=2048).

Pass the row count to the kernel as its own argument (nrows_x, the rows of this slice) and use it for the
three row bounds (bias prefetch, PTQ1_0 warp-per-row path, store). Same fix as ggml-org/llama.cpp#32159
(argument form asked for in its review); PrismML fixed the same race in their tree in #415.

(cherry picked from commit 74a312d0c43d922656df9a333c3db6144cc1cd5c)
